 "sections": [
  {
   "heading": "What was predicted",
   "body": "Rebuilds U.S. businesses as populations of firms, one population per sector. Each period a firm that does not use AI may start, and a firm that uses it may stop, with hazards that follow a diffusion curve: firms imitate adopters in their own sector and in the whole economy, and growth can slow as fewer non-users remain. From each cutoff the simulation carries every sector forward and is scored against the share of firms that actually reported AI use three and six months later. The alternative asks how much faster manufacturing and retail would adopt if an adoption programme doubled their firms' hazard of starting.",
